| `test_quality.assertions.roots` | list of strings | `["tests"]` in keel and in a generated project; absent, the same value, which its reader reports as `[using default] test_quality.assertions.roots = ["tests"]` | a non-empty list of relative POSIX directories, no empty, `.` or `..` part | `tests/assertion_quality.py` (`policy`, `test_files`), called by `tests/integration/test_assertion_quality_gate.py`, through `scripts/config_loader.py`'s `test_quality.assertions.roots` row | Moves which directories the assertion-quality gate reads test functions from, by pytest's default names (`test_*.py` or `*_test.py`; `test*` functions, at module level including compound statements, or in a `Test*` class or a `unittest.TestCase` subclass, including local inheritance and nested test classes), and which modules a test's helper may live in: a helper in a file outside every root is never followed, so a test that asserts only through one fails as having no assertion. Each configured root must exist and yield at least one test file; a missing or empty root fails naming that root. A scan over zero test functions fails. An empty list or a `..` part fails the gate with `SourceTreeError`, preserving the loader's diagnostic lines and naming this key. | a pytest selection: `make test` still runs every test under `tests` | always |
